 ## Background
-Originated by Chaoli Wang, Jinzhu Gao, and Han-Wei Shen from The Ohio State University and Oak Ridge National Laboratory [S1][S2]. An abbreviated version appeared in Eurographics Symposium on Parallel Graphics and Visualization 2004 (EGPGV2004) [S1]. The full paper was presented at PC 2005 [S1]. It addresses the challenge of visualizing large-scale scientific data (e.g., Richtmyer-Meshkov Instability) on parallel architectures by combining wavelet-based multiresolution representation with a novel data distribution scheme to eliminate inter-processor dependencies and balance load [S1][S2].
